Subject: Enforce context-local rotation and synchronized native logging

Pinned API: llama.cpp a34de861 (b12015), after 0004 decode lifecycle hooks.
Context creation must not mutate the process environment or shared model state.
Append an explicit context preference and apply it only during synchronous
memory construction, including nested KV caches, using scoped thread-local state.
Existing environment and model opt-outs remain honored.

llama/ggml logger pairs were unsynchronized, and common/fit published pointers
to stack-local logger scopes process-wide. Move the shared pair behind its own
mutex, snapshot before callbacks, and make fit overrides thread-local. Raw logger
users still retain user_data through in-flight calls. No lock spans a callback.

ABI: append one bool to the context params after the mandatory decode hooks;
all earlier field offsets are unchanged. runtime_safety_abi_v1 is required by the
Rust backend and context wrappers so stale/unpatched libraries fail to link.
The new ggml log functions are additive C ABI entries used by core and fit.

